hysical and Economic Development Committee Meeting Expired\nEvents for October\n8th\nNo Events\nEvents for October\n9th\nNo Events\nEvents for October\n10th\nNo Events\nEvents for October\n11th\nNo Events\nEvents for October\n12th\nAll Day\nColumbus Day – Holiday – County is Closed Expired\nEvents for October\n13th\nNo Events\nEvents for October\n14th\n9:30 am - 10:00 am\nBoard of Commissioners Meeting Expired\n10:00 am - 10:30 am\nPublic Safety and Judicial Committee Meeting Expired\nEvents for October\n15th\nNo Events\nEvents for October\n16th\nNo Events\nEvents for October\n17th\nNo Events\nEvents for October\n18th\nNo Events\nEvents for October\n19th\nNo Events\nEvents for October\n20th\nNo Events\nEvents for October\n21st\n8:30 am - 9:00 am\nFinance Committee Meeting\n9:30 am - 10:00 am\nBoard of Commissioners Meeting\n10:00 am - 10:30 am\nHealth Education and Human Services Committee Meeting\nEvents for October\n22nd\nNo Events\nEvents for October\n23rd\nNo Events\nEvents for October\n24th\nNo Events\nEvents for October\n25th\nNo Events\nEvents for October\n26th\nNo Events\nEvents for October\n27th\nNo Events\nEvents for October\n28th\nNo Events\nEvents for October\n29th\nNo Events\nEvents for October\n30th\nNo Events\nEvents for October\n31st\nNo Events\nAbout\nNewaygo County\nNewaygo County was named after Chippewa Indian Chief: Naw-wa-goo, one of the signers of the Treaty of Saginaw in 1812. The county has over 230 natural lakes and over 350 miles of rivers and streams. Three huge dams were built after the turn of the century: Croton, Hardy and Newaygo. Croton and Hardy Dams remain today, with Hardy the largest earthen dam east of the Mississippi.\nToday Newaygo County relies on tourism as its main economic support, with agriculture and small manufacturing secondary. The Muskegon River continues to be the main attraction for summer cottage residents and fishermen, who find it nearly the best source for steelhead in the spring and salmon in the fall anywhere in Michigan. Hunting, camping and RV’ing are also excellent, as over half the county is contained in the Manistee National Forest.\nNeed Help?\nPostal Correspondence Address\nNewaygo County Government\n1087 Newell St, P.O. Box 885\nWhite Cloud MI 49349\nPhone Directory\nEmergency Alerts\nAlert Sign Up\nDisclaimer\nPrivacy Policy\nDisclaimer\nPrivacy Policy\nAll content herein © Newaygo County 2020",
